package dev.kstep.geometry

import dev.kstep.geometry.select.EdgeSelector
import dev.kstep.geometry.select.FaceSelector

/**
 * Sources of edges generated by DERIVED features (Welle N2, ADR-0034): a fillet or chamfer, a boolean, a hole.
 * Like the profile sources of ADR-0033 they name the INPUT of the operation, not the geometry it produced: "the
 * edges I rounded", "the faces of the drill", "the section of both bodies". They are resolved against the
 * operands of the operation (never against its result) and mapped to result edges with OCCT's own `Generated()`
 * history, read from the same maker as the edge history. Use them with `GeneratedEdges`.
 *
 * Which source fits which operation, and the role of its images, is checked structurally before any native
 * call (see [GeneratedRole]):
 *
 * * fillet / chamfer: [BlendedEdges], [OperandEdges] with role [GeneratedRole.BOUNDARY]
 * * boolean: [BooleanSection], [OperandFaces] with role [GeneratedRole.SECTION]
 * * hole: [HoleWall], [BooleanSection], [OperandFaces] with role [GeneratedRole.SECTION]; [HoleWall] also with
 *   [GeneratedRole.RIM_ENTRY] and [GeneratedRole.RIM_EXIT]
 * * shell (INWARD only, ADR-0041): [ShellInnerEdges], [ShellInnerFaces] with role [GeneratedRole.CAVITY]
 */
sealed interface DerivedGenerationSource : GenerationSource

/**
 * The edges of operand [operand] (always 0, the filleted / chamfered shape) that [selector] picks on that operand.
 * Role BOUNDARY: the edges that border the blend surface and a face the operation did not create. Only valid for a
 * fillet or chamfer; OCCT reports no edge for an edge of a boolean (it reports vertices, ADR-0034 spike G3).
 */
data class OperandEdges(
    val operand: Int = 0,
    val selector: EdgeSelector,
) : DerivedGenerationSource

/**
 * The faces [selector] picks on operand [operand] (0 = left / base shape, 1 = right operand or the drill of a
 * hole). Role SECTION: the edges where those faces were cut by the other body.
 */
data class OperandFaces(
    val operand: Int,
    val selector: FaceSelector,
) : DerivedGenerationSource

/** Every edge a fillet or chamfer acted on. Role BOUNDARY. */
data object BlendedEdges : DerivedGenerationSource

/** All faces of both operands of a boolean or hole, i.e. every section edge between the two bodies. Role SECTION. */
data object BooleanSection : DerivedGenerationSource

/**
 * The lateral face of the drill of a hole. Roles: SECTION (all edges where the wall meets the body), RIM_ENTRY (the
 * ring at which the drill enters) and RIM_EXIT (the ring at which it leaves; empty for a blind hole, which makes
 * the name fail instead of guessing).
 * RIM_ENTRY and RIM_EXIT also fail with an EdgeNamingException when the drill breaks out through a side face or
 * the rings are ambiguous; SECTION stays usable then and is the fallback.
 */
data object HoleWall : DerivedGenerationSource

/**
 * INWARD shell only (ADR-0041): the edges [selector] picks on the INPUT of the shell. Role CAVITY: the inner copy of
 * each of them, i.e. the matching edge of the cavity wall. The selector is evaluated on the shell's input at every
 * rebuild, so `Edges.parallel(Z)` keeps meaning "the inner copies of the vertical edges" when the body grows. An
 * input edge that borders only opened faces has no inner copy and fails the name instead of being guessed.
 */
data class ShellInnerEdges(
    val selector: EdgeSelector,
) : DerivedGenerationSource

/**
 * INWARD shell only (ADR-0041): the faces [selector] picks on the INPUT of the shell. Role CAVITY: every edge that
 * bounds the inner copy of such a face (the matching wall of the cavity). A face that was opened has no inner copy
 * (it becomes the rim face) and fails the name instead of being guessed.
 */
data class ShellInnerFaces(
    val selector: FaceSelector,
) : DerivedGenerationSource
